# Normalise line endings. The working tree currently mixes CRLF and LF
# (21 of 53 source files are CRLF), which makes diffs noisy and makes
# whole-file rewrites look like whole-file changes.
#
# `text=auto` stores everything as LF in the repository and checks out the
# platform-native ending. Run `git add --renormalize .` once to apply.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and anything read by a Linux container must stay LF even on
# Windows checkouts, or the shebang breaks.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be munged.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary

# Lockfiles are generated; collapse them in diffs and reviews.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
